<section class="bg-sand" id="private">
  <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Private whole boat charter</span>
      <h2>$3,900 per night</h2>
      <p>The entire vessel with a professional Captain and Mate. Limited to 6 paying guests under U.S. Coast Guard rules for uninspected passenger vessels. Minimum 2 nights, 3 days.</p>
      <h3>Includes</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Captain and mate</li>
        <li>4 paddleboards and 2 kayaks</li>
        <li>15 foot tender for shore excursions</li>
        <li>Self catered: you bring and prepare your own food and beverages</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card">
      <h3>Private chef add on</h3>
      <p>Chef, chef prepared meals, house beer, wine and standard spirits. Per night:</p>
      <table class="rate-table">
        <tr><td>2 guests</td><td>$800</td></tr>
        <tr><td>4 guests</td><td>$1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>6 guests</td><td>$1,200</td></tr>
      </table>
      <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Optional add ons</h3>
      <table class="rate-table">
        <tr><td>Landing craft (diving, biking, cargo, live boat dive support)</td><td>$500/night</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Divemaster (optional, or dive self guided)</td><td>$500/night</td></tr>
      </table>
      <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Additional charges</h3>
      <table class="rate-table">
        <tr><td>Cleaning fee (one time)</td><td>$400</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Damage deposit (refundable)</td><td>$500</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fuel deposit (settled at trip end)</td><td>$1,000</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="dry-boat">
  <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Dry boat charter</span>
      <h2>$3,400 per night</h2>
      <p>For experienced captains. An unmanned private recreational charter with exclusive use of Supernova, paddleboards, kayaks, tender and all standard equipment. You provide food, beverages and fuel and handle all cooking and operations.</p>
      <h3>Captain requirements</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>Pre qualification and approval before booking</li>
        <li>Mandatory orientation on all systems and operations</li>
        <li>Captain Paul on call 24/7 by phone or radio</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Capacity</h3>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>8 guests in 4 private staterooms</li>
        <li>4 more on inflatable mattresses on the top deck</li>
        <li>More than 6 guests allowed under recreational boating rules, with safety gear provided for your declared count</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card">
      <h3>Skipper training add on</h3>
      <p class="from">$500 <small>per night</small></p>
      <p>A licensed USCG 100 ton Master aboard when underway with daily training sessions. Not staying on the vessel, but available 24/7 and nearby throughout the trip.</p>
      <h4>Daily training topics</h4>
      <ul class="checklist" style="font-size:.95rem">
        <li>Navigation and chart plotting</li>
        <li>Boat handling and anchoring</li>
        <li>Trip and route planning</li>
        <li>Watermaker and freshwater systems</li>
        <li>Battery and energy management</li>
        <li>Systems and routine maintenance</li>
        <li>Waste and sewage management</li>
        <li>Marine radio operation</li>
        <li>Emergency preparedness and safety</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 style="margin-top:22px">Additional charges</h3>
      <table class="rate-table">
        <tr><td>Damage deposit (refundable)</td><td>$1,000</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fuel deposit (settled at trip end)</td><td>$400/day</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

